{{!-- Portrait left; the name, and under it the one line that says what this kind of item IS
      (`item-sheet.js`, SUBTYPE_HINT), to the right of it.

      No tag row. The tags belong on an inventory line, where they tell two carried things apart
      at a glance — on the item's own sheet they repeat what the fields below them already say,
      in a window that has room for neither. The line that replaced them is the one thing the
      sheet cannot say anywhere else.

      The name is ink on paper inside a drawn box, not paper reversed out of a solid slab. The
      character sheet stopped shouting its name out of a black block for the reason this one
      stopped too: a sheet already carrying inked caps reads as a web form with a title bar the
      moment a solid block lands at the top of it. The box is the same mark the Gold chip wears,
      at the same weight. --}}
<header class="item-header">
    <img class="portrait" src="{{item.img}}" data-action="editImage" data-edit="img" data-tooltip="{{item.name}}" />
    <input class="name-input" type="text" name="name" value="{{item.name}}" placeholder="{{localize 'CAIRN.Name'}}"
        data-ink="box" data-ink-seed="item-name" data-ink-w="1.6" />
    {{#if isFeature}}
    {{!-- The feature's one property, where a caption would go: whether it is a Critical Damage
          clause. The NPC's Features tab draws the words for a flagged one. --}}
    <div class="item-header-critical cairn-field">
        <label for="feature-critical-{{item.id}}">{{localize 'CAIRN.CriticalDamageFull'}}</label>
        {{> "systems/cairn2e/templates/parts/toggle.hbs" field="system.critical" value=system.critical
            id=(concat "feature-critical-" item.id)}}
    </div>
    {{else if hint}}
    <p class="item-header-hint">{{localize hint}}</p>
    {{/if}}
</header>
